WEBVTT

00:00:02.020 --> 00:00:05.000
12:40 P.M. Nature District, Okutama

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:09.050
The students at Musashi Ariadust Academy

00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:11.440
are beginning to rebel.

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:13.870
They wish to hold a special meeting

00:00:13.870 --> 00:00:16.800
to pass a vote of no confidence in you.

00:00:19.730 --> 00:00:21.970
Do you understand what you must do?

00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:27.800
Go negotiate with them so that the outcome

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:29.210
for Musashi is favorable.

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:35.050
Mitotsudaira?

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:36.990
Naomasa?

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:05.250
What do you see?

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:05.250
Nani ga mieru?

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:08.670
You've closed yourself off to love

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:08.670
Ari no mama no kimi wa

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:14.560
Until you grow innately strong

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:14.560
Tsuyoku naru made itoshisa wo tojite

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:17.640
What are you listening to?

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:17.640
Nani wo kiku no?

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:20.730
Shall I tell you about days long past

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:20.730
Himitsu no kobeya de

00:01:20.730 --> 00:01:26.570
In our secret little room?

00:01:20.730 --> 00:01:26.570
Inishie no hibi katarou ka?

00:01:26.790 --> 00:01:29.780
Embraced in memories

00:01:26.790 --> 00:01:29.780
Kioku ni dakarete

00:01:29.780 --> 00:01:33.070
The mysteria crumbles

00:01:29.780 --> 00:01:33.070
Kudakareta mysteria

00:01:33.070 --> 00:01:35.830
Once you overcome this tragedy

00:01:33.070 --> 00:01:35.830
Higeki wo koete

00:01:35.830 --> 00:01:38.040
Offer a gentle prayer

00:01:35.830 --> 00:01:38.040
Odayaka na inori

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:42.060
Endings are just beginnings

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:42.060
Owari ga hajimari

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:45.250
People toss aside all they have

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:45.250
Shinsekai de hito wa mirai wo

00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:47.840
Without ever knowing

00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:47.840
Bishu no you ni

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:51.310
If they could drink up the new world

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:51.310
Nomi hoseru ka sae shirazu

00:01:51.310 --> 00:01:54.470
Like a savory wine

00:01:51.310 --> 00:01:54.470
Subete houri nageta

00:01:54.470 --> 00:01:57.630
The new world resides

00:01:54.470 --> 00:01:57.630
Shinsekai wa tsumetai risei to

00:01:57.630 --> 00:02:00.350
Kiseki no hazama

00:01:57.630 --> 00:02:00.350
Between boring logic and miracles

00:02:00.630 --> 00:02:09.360
Doushite koko de kimi to aeta no

00:02:00.630 --> 00:02:09.360
I wonder why this is where I first met you

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:18.800
12:50 P.M.
Azuma and Miriam's Room, Okutama

00:02:14.550 --> 00:02:16.900
Uh, ummm...

00:02:22.670 --> 00:02:25.330
It's okay. You'll be okay.

00:02:23.180 --> 00:02:28.020
"Musashi's Knights"

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:30.960
How does it feel to become a daddy overnight?

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:33.540
Miriam!

00:02:33.710 --> 00:02:36.960
Oh, sorry! This was your bed, wasn't it?

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:38.720
I don't mind.

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:42.820
More importantly, two Far East guards
are keeping watch outside.

00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:44.680
Now why is that?

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:47.890
Uh, I wonder why...

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:52.150
You never mentioned that you are
the crown prince, now did you?

00:02:52.540 --> 00:02:56.170
No, not anymore! I've returned to secular life!

00:02:56.170 --> 00:02:58.290
I'm just an ordinary commoner!

00:02:58.290 --> 00:03:00.490
People won't see you as such.

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:03.740
There is a great deal of unrest out there.

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:06.860
All of our classmates who are clashing
with the Testament Union

00:03:06.860 --> 00:03:08.930
wish to hold a special meeting in an attempt

00:03:08.930 --> 00:03:12.960
to determine Musashi and the Far East's course of action.

00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:14.380
Then we must-

00:03:14.380 --> 00:03:16.590
Try to consider the situation you're in!

00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:20.300
Why do you think you're being watched?

00:03:20.610 --> 00:03:22.510
The Testament Union intends to take

00:03:22.510 --> 00:03:25.390
advantage of the situation and conquer the Far East.

00:03:25.390 --> 00:03:27.410
Kyoto is inviolable and the

00:03:27.410 --> 00:03:30.060
Emperor sustains the world, so his son's actions...

00:03:31.570 --> 00:03:34.520
I could sway people at the very least.

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:37.870
Let's believe in everyone.

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:41.340
1:00 P.M.
Musashi Ariadust Academy

00:03:39.630 --> 00:03:42.440
I am confident they will choose what is best

00:03:42.440 --> 00:03:44.320
for Musashi and the Far East.

00:03:47.250 --> 00:03:50.080
Now then, it looks like we're all here.

00:03:51.110 --> 00:03:55.290
I am Masazumi Honda, Vice-president of
Musashi Ariadust Academy's Student Council.

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:57.970
I condone this special meeting and came

00:03:57.970 --> 00:04:00.290
to make a proposal for all students.

00:04:00.570 --> 00:04:02.260
May I ask you something?

00:04:02.620 --> 00:04:06.010
Why did Naomasa and Mitotsudaira side with you?

00:04:06.280 --> 00:04:08.440
If we defy the Provisional Council,

00:04:08.440 --> 00:04:11.130
we could end up
in a war with the Testament Union.

00:04:11.590 --> 00:04:15.260
So the Engineering Club sent me to see

00:04:15.260 --> 00:04:18.310
if we're strong enough to hold our own.

00:04:18.610 --> 00:04:24.590
Likewise. It is a knight's duty
to protect the people and the land.

00:04:24.990 --> 00:04:28.300
We want to avoid doing something that could cost lives.

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:30.740
Thus I sided as I did to ascertain as much.

00:04:35.910 --> 00:04:37.580
I'm former Treasurer,

00:04:38.510 --> 00:04:40.090
Shirojiro Bertoni.

00:04:40.320 --> 00:04:41.680
I'm glad you came.

00:04:42.040 --> 00:04:46.280
We have received permission from all of the students

00:04:46.280 --> 00:04:49.440
to determine the fate of Musashi during this meeting.

00:04:49.850 --> 00:04:54.390
Why the hell is Tori wrapped in a curtain?

00:04:54.390 --> 00:04:55.640
Is he a spring roll?

00:04:55.640 --> 00:04:56.480
He's a dumpling.

00:04:56.480 --> 00:04:59.970
Nope! I'm a sushi roll!

00:04:59.970 --> 00:05:01.650
The nori is white, so rice-

00:05:02.090 --> 00:05:02.690
Shut up!

00:05:04.560 --> 00:05:06.200
Roll, roll, roll...

00:05:05.180 --> 00:05:06.180
Censored

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:08.450
Roll me up!

00:05:08.450 --> 00:05:10.950
Be as gentle as a mom! C'mon!

00:05:12.670 --> 00:05:14.460
Mommy!

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:19.240
Now then, the agenda is to pass the vote
regarding my no confidence

00:05:19.240 --> 00:05:21.940
and determine the Academy's stance, correct?

00:05:21.940 --> 00:05:22.670
Correct.

00:05:23.110 --> 00:05:25.250
So you'll represent the Testament Union

00:05:25.250 --> 00:05:27.380
and we'll represent Musashi.

00:05:27.870 --> 00:05:30.670
Political trouble is supervised by students and normal citizens

00:05:30.670 --> 00:05:32.560
may not participate.

00:05:33.160 --> 00:05:35.480
That's the way of the world right now.

00:05:35.880 --> 00:05:40.930
Now that both sides have made their stances clear,
let's get this started!

00:05:41.320 --> 00:05:45.120
T..the Testament Union and Musashi
get three representatives each.

00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:47.230
Whoever wins two rounds is victorious.

00:05:47.230 --> 00:05:51.120
Musashi Ariadust Academy
will consent to whichever side wins.

00:05:51.530 --> 00:05:52.930
If the Testament Union wins,

00:05:52.930 --> 00:05:55.800
we will accept Horizon's death
and Musashi's new leadership.

00:05:55.800 --> 00:05:58.620
If Musashi wins, we will go save Horizon.

00:05:59.010 --> 00:06:02.780
You may face off through battle,
negotiation or whatever.

00:06:02.780 --> 00:06:06.960
The Testament Union must somehow prove
that defiance is senseless.

00:06:06.960 --> 00:06:10.260
Musashi must prove that they can fight back.

00:06:10.790 --> 00:06:12.920
Does that sound about right?

00:06:12.920 --> 00:06:13.810
Judge!

00:06:14.220 --> 00:06:15.090
Then I shall go-

00:06:15.090 --> 00:06:16.590
I'm up first.

00:06:17.750 --> 00:06:20.000
Defying the Testament Union aside,

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:24.980
Musashi lacks explicit weaponry,
so show me how you plan to fight.

00:06:25.050 --> 00:06:25.710
Confirm

00:06:25.730 --> 00:06:26.960
Contact!

00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:39.220
It's the God of War, Jizuri Suzaku.

00:06:39.800 --> 00:06:41.480
It's made up of Gods of War parts

00:06:41.480 --> 00:06:44.130
found on some battlefields down below.

00:06:44.790 --> 00:06:46.820
My mouse currently inhabits it.

00:06:46.820 --> 00:06:48.880
It's the Engineering Club's pride and joy.

00:06:49.090 --> 00:06:51.760
Lady Naomasa's awfully pumped up...

00:06:51.760 --> 00:06:54.260
Jeez, there's no surviving this one!

00:06:54.780 --> 00:06:56.870
Hey, Shiro! You go.

00:06:56.870 --> 00:06:58.230
Oh, you're back.

00:06:58.500 --> 00:07:01.270
S..Sir Tori, you're putting a merchant

00:07:01.270 --> 00:07:03.690
like Sir Shirojiro up against that?!

00:07:03.950 --> 00:07:06.070
What're you thinking?!

00:07:07.050 --> 00:07:08.650
Don't you get it, Tenzo?

00:07:09.290 --> 00:07:10.900
I hate him.

00:07:11.120 --> 00:07:11.860
Wha-?!

00:07:12.170 --> 00:07:13.880
Y..you monster!

00:07:13.880 --> 00:07:15.870
You're truly horrible!

00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:19.830
But this damn merchant's always
dissing me out, ya know?

00:07:20.090 --> 00:07:24.170
Suffer a little and reflect on the error of your ways!

00:07:24.500 --> 00:07:29.390
Oh, so if I win, everything I've said is proven true.

00:07:29.390 --> 00:07:30.840
What a bargain.

00:07:30.840 --> 00:07:34.970
What's this? You seem eager to fight.

00:07:35.180 --> 00:07:38.040
The bigger the risk, the bigger the reward.

00:07:38.040 --> 00:07:40.800
I'll get to purchase the Engineering Club's trust

00:07:40.800 --> 00:07:43.100
and prove we can resist the Gods of War.

00:07:46.760 --> 00:07:50.460
Naomasa, according to my spell's contract,

00:07:50.460 --> 00:07:52.280
I need Heidi's support as a broker.

00:07:52.660 --> 00:07:53.840
Is that acceptable?

00:07:53.840 --> 00:07:56.230
Judge, I don't mind.

00:07:57.320 --> 00:08:00.000
Assuming that will help you defeat this!

00:08:00.370 --> 00:08:01.370
I'm going all-out!

00:08:10.760 --> 00:08:13.040
What the hell is that spell?

00:08:13.040 --> 00:08:15.300
I guess you could call it a spell.

00:08:15.820 --> 00:08:17.530
Collection 3-Improved              Collection 3-Improved
Assemble                                 Assemble

00:08:18.940 --> 00:08:21.480
It's actually much more simplistic:

00:08:20.910 --> 00:08:23.310
tnemyaP

00:08:21.990 --> 00:08:23.310
The power of money.

00:08:23.310 --> 00:08:26.650
Payment

00:08:23.550 --> 00:08:27.240
My contract is with the God of Commerce, Sanct,

00:08:27.240 --> 00:08:32.320
who can cover other gods' exchanges through commerce.

00:08:32.550 --> 00:08:37.570
He's paying for 150 guards' worth
of "workforce" by the hour.

00:08:37.830 --> 00:08:40.590
The guards receive protection from the God of Labor,

00:08:40.590 --> 00:08:42.060
so the rest is easy.

00:08:42.060 --> 00:08:43.660
It's just mediation work.

00:08:43.880 --> 00:08:48.670
Right now I can focus the
strength of 150 guards in one spot.

00:08:49.510 --> 00:08:51.850
If you convert it to weight, that's 10.5 tons.

00:08:52.300 --> 00:08:55.970
It's enough for me to fight against
your 10-ton class God of War.

00:08:57.540 --> 00:08:58.850
That even the score?

00:09:01.800 --> 00:09:02.850
I guess so.

00:09:03.530 --> 00:09:05.140
In that case,

00:09:05.910 --> 00:09:07.730
let's fight!

00:09:15.510 --> 00:09:17.990
<i>Shiro, don't worry about the town!</i>

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:19.730
<i>I made a deal with the Engineering Club.</i>

00:09:18.010 --> 00:09:24.060
Divine
Transmission

00:09:19.730 --> 00:09:21.590
<i>They'll stop any of Jizuri Suzaku's "labor" directed</i>

00:09:21.590 --> 00:09:23.740
<i>at the buildings from making contact.</i>

00:09:27.150 --> 00:09:31.050
Much obliged! So I can truly go wild.

00:09:37.440 --> 00:09:41.260
Shirojiro, why did you decide
to oppose the Testament Union?

00:09:41.750 --> 00:09:44.080
Even if they take over the Far East,

00:09:44.080 --> 00:09:47.020
you could still restart your business and live in peace!

00:09:47.250 --> 00:09:48.740
My reasoning is simple.

00:09:52.460 --> 00:09:54.780
Let's discuss money for a moment.

00:09:55.490 --> 00:09:57.580
At present, countless countries

00:09:57.580 --> 00:10:00.000
have taken vast loans from the Far East

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:04.160
so they can re-create history
and maintain their provisional rule.

00:10:04.620 --> 00:10:07.250
So they took loans; so what?!

00:10:09.980 --> 00:10:11.000
You see...

00:10:11.000 --> 00:10:13.050
banks across the Far East hold money

00:10:13.050 --> 00:10:16.840
the country earned through honest commerce and transportation

00:10:16.840 --> 00:10:20.260
along with taxing their foreign settlements.

00:10:20.580 --> 00:10:23.590
But if the Far East falls under totalitarian rule,

00:10:23.590 --> 00:10:26.520
they'll lose all that and the debt will go unpaid.

00:10:26.890 --> 00:10:28.230
Then there's Musashi!

00:10:30.740 --> 00:10:33.850
As Musashi isn't under another country's provisional rule,

00:10:33.850 --> 00:10:37.860
people everywhere are donating their
pocket change to Asama Shrine

00:10:38.200 --> 00:10:41.760
and saving up their blessings for external energy.

00:10:42.680 --> 00:10:46.970
In brief, Musashi is becoming the
Far East's largest energy storehouse.

00:10:49.100 --> 00:10:50.850
Now listen up!

00:10:51.680 --> 00:10:53.110
Musashi can fight!

00:10:54.200 --> 00:10:58.720
We can as long as Musashi continues
to fly and collect money!

00:10:59.040 --> 00:11:01.050
Wow, that's impressive.

00:11:01.050 --> 00:11:04.180
You'd never know he spends his days
counting his money with a grin.

00:11:04.420 --> 00:11:05.870
You bet!

00:11:05.870 --> 00:11:10.310
Shiro plays wonderfully dirty when it comes to money,

00:11:10.310 --> 00:11:12.400
but he has lots of other good traits.

00:11:12.400 --> 00:11:12.810
Huh?

00:11:12.810 --> 00:11:16.150
He always goes to the living room
once he finishes work,

00:11:16.150 --> 00:11:19.950
he turns around to make sure I'm keeping up
when we're out walking,

00:11:19.950 --> 00:11:21.970
he listens to my problems,

00:11:21.240 --> 00:11:23.970
Uh, um... Hello?

00:11:21.970 --> 00:11:26.490
and plays super dirty with me in the simplest of ways.

00:11:28.740 --> 00:11:29.620
But...

00:11:30.220 --> 00:11:33.630
I play super dirty with him, too.

00:11:34.200 --> 00:11:35.380
That's nothing, Shirojiro!

00:11:35.900 --> 00:11:39.970
No, I'll use the nickname the
Testament Union gave you: Poker Face!

00:11:49.810 --> 00:11:51.310
That's a wrap.

00:11:57.510 --> 00:11:58.480
Impossible!

00:11:58.720 --> 00:12:00.000
How'd you do that?!

00:12:00.970 --> 00:12:03.070
That cost more than anticipated.

00:12:10.610 --> 00:12:11.500
The building...!

00:12:21.070 --> 00:12:22.760
What just happened?

00:12:22.760 --> 00:12:24.050
It's quite simple:

00:12:24.840 --> 00:12:26.760
I bought it.

00:12:26.960 --> 00:12:28.150
That's absurd!

00:12:28.150 --> 00:12:29.890
This is a densely populated area!

00:12:30.530 --> 00:12:31.850
Look up there.

00:12:33.060 --> 00:12:36.490
The rumor about Musashi's change in
power has scared them away.

00:12:36.490 --> 00:12:38.830
Naturally, available real estate is increasing.

00:12:38.830 --> 00:12:43.440
All I had to do was obtain some land and lead you to it.

00:12:45.060 --> 00:12:47.780
So you had this all planned out?

00:12:48.210 --> 00:12:51.760
What do you want from the Engineering Club?

00:12:51.760 --> 00:12:52.840
Work.

00:12:53.380 --> 00:12:57.420
For Musashi to collect money,
it must continue flying.

00:12:58.570 --> 00:13:03.420
As such, you're our ally, Naomasa.

00:13:09.270 --> 00:13:12.470
Heidi, we need help lifting up
the God of War,

00:13:12.470 --> 00:13:13.950
<i>but keep it cheap.</i>

00:13:13.960 --> 00:13:14.900
Okay!

00:13:18.510 --> 00:13:20.560
Okay, next up is...

00:13:20.560 --> 00:13:22.780
Judge, it is I.

00:13:23.300 --> 00:13:25.290
As representative of Musashi's knights,

00:13:25.290 --> 00:13:28.780
I, Argent Loup Nate Mitotsudaira must ask:

00:13:29.340 --> 00:13:33.540
The Far East lacks a sovereign, so how do you

00:13:33.540 --> 00:13:36.290
intend to make us knights obey you?

00:13:36.630 --> 00:13:38.480
Come and face me!

00:13:43.070 --> 00:13:45.780
1:35 P.M.
Execution Grounds, Inquisition Warship

00:13:46.070 --> 00:13:47.740
Metal-Style Traditional Songs
MAN-YOU
For Beginners

00:13:46.970 --> 00:13:49.650
<i>Lady Horizon, how do you feel?</i>

00:13:50.050 --> 00:13:54.150
Judge. Bluntly put, nothing is wrong.

00:13:54.150 --> 00:13:55.520
Was there a problem?

00:13:55.520 --> 00:14:00.140
<i>No. We are currently scanning you,</i>

00:14:00.140 --> 00:14:01.990
<i>so I wanted to see if you're okay.</i>

00:14:02.260 --> 00:14:03.690
You are?

00:14:07.110 --> 00:14:09.450
Is it okay for me to wear my clothes?

00:14:10.790 --> 00:14:11.700
<i>Tes.</i>

00:14:12.270 --> 00:14:15.270
I see. I am glad to hear it.

00:14:16.550 --> 00:14:19.880
Master Muneshige, won't Musashi's special council meeting

00:14:18.940 --> 00:14:23.730
Tres España

00:14:19.880 --> 00:14:22.950
end before the princess must commit suicide?

00:14:22.950 --> 00:14:23.750
Probably.

00:14:24.390 --> 00:14:27.960
Then Master Muneshige, if we go to war,

00:14:27.960 --> 00:14:31.870
we'll be forced to fight with nothing more than our current forces.

00:14:32.230 --> 00:14:33.310
Don't worry.

00:14:34.010 --> 00:14:36.310
We still have more students than them.

00:14:36.840 --> 00:14:38.020
Right.

00:14:38.020 --> 00:14:40.270
But we can't let our guard down.

00:14:40.790 --> 00:14:43.520
Musashi's Supreme Federation
and Student Council are operational.

00:14:44.050 --> 00:14:48.120
And don't forget that the Far East has Shinto spells.

00:14:48.420 --> 00:14:50.860
Shinto spells?

00:14:50.860 --> 00:14:55.420
Tes. As you just saw, Shintoists can manipulate any

00:14:55.420 --> 00:15:02.130
spell so long as they can pay offerings to their god.

00:15:04.480 --> 00:15:06.960
That could prove somewhat troublesome.

00:15:09.330 --> 00:15:13.020
Well? Who will try to make the knights defer to you?

00:15:13.020 --> 00:15:14.990
Jeez, what should we do?

00:15:15.430 --> 00:15:18.470
Nate looks super fired up, ya know?

00:15:18.470 --> 00:15:21.980
Hm? Neshinbara, whatcha think?

00:15:22.360 --> 00:15:26.610
Ah, well, this has been nagging at me.

00:15:27.060 --> 00:15:30.020
Knights are higher class than us commoners.

00:15:30.020 --> 00:15:32.280
So why would she want to face us?

00:15:32.490 --> 00:15:34.470
That's bugging me, too.

00:15:34.820 --> 00:15:38.250
And aren't Musashi's knights feudal knights?

00:15:38.250 --> 00:15:43.420
So then, basically, Nate's higher ranking than us and

00:15:43.420 --> 00:15:45.630
she's supposed to protect us, right?

00:15:46.030 --> 00:15:47.010
Judge.

00:15:47.010 --> 00:15:50.210
Doesn't that mean she has a reason for facing us?

00:15:50.210 --> 00:15:54.890
As such, Nate will join us if we clear that test.

00:15:56.460 --> 00:15:57.350
In that case...

00:16:01.050 --> 00:16:02.810
What is keeping you?

00:16:03.030 --> 00:16:05.160
Could you hurry it up?

00:16:05.500 --> 00:16:06.510
Sweet!

00:16:12.320 --> 00:16:13.610
Wha-?!

00:16:13.850 --> 00:16:16.290
Wait, what's going on?

00:16:17.150 --> 00:16:22.080
Uh, I was hoping to square off with someone...

00:16:22.500 --> 00:16:27.380
Um, I..I ch..chose to come up.

00:16:27.690 --> 00:16:30.980
I thought I'd be appropriate...

00:16:30.980 --> 00:16:31.970
Suzu...

00:16:31.970 --> 00:16:34.470
<i>No, did they figure it out?!</i>

00:16:35.230 --> 00:16:37.340
<i>Our presence as knights may strengthen</i>

00:16:37.340 --> 00:16:41.440
<i>the masses' desire to defy the Testament Union.</i>

00:16:41.440 --> 00:16:43.480
<i>But should they fight, </i>

00:16:43.480 --> 00:16:47.200
<i>it would be nigh impossible
for us to protect Musashi on our own.</i>

00:16:47.200 --> 00:16:50.220
<i>If we place the people's safety first,</i>

00:16:50.220 --> 00:16:52.820
<i>we must surrender to the Testament Union.</i>

00:16:52.820 --> 00:16:54.560
<i>In other words...</i>

00:16:58.000 --> 00:17:00.790
As representative of Musashi's Knights and nobility,

00:17:01.300 --> 00:17:04.250
I, Nate Mitotsudaira, have a proclamation.

00:17:05.560 --> 00:17:06.790
This isn't good.

00:17:06.790 --> 00:17:08.090
Mukai, stop her!

00:17:08.320 --> 00:17:11.800
Musashi's knights want her to fight a civilian and lose!

00:17:12.010 --> 00:17:13.690
What's with that?

00:17:13.690 --> 00:17:18.420
If she loses,
it'll be 2-to-1 and Musashi wins.

00:17:18.420 --> 00:17:20.780
This isn't about winning or losing anymore.

00:17:20.780 --> 00:17:23.360
If the knights bow down to us commoners,

00:17:23.360 --> 00:17:25.940
they'll give up their social status.

00:17:24.180 --> 00:17:25.940
All of Musashi's knights...

00:17:25.940 --> 00:17:28.940
In other words, Musashi will lose its knights!

00:17:29.230 --> 00:17:31.840
Musashi wouldn't be able to fight even if we wanted to.

00:17:30.610 --> 00:17:32.610
...acknowledge that the people of Musashi have...

00:17:32.840 --> 00:17:35.650
Hey, Bell! Could you stop Nate?

00:17:37.010 --> 00:17:38.480
Anything works!

00:17:39.660 --> 00:17:41.450
Wh..what should I do?

00:17:42.500 --> 00:17:43.830
Grope her boobs!

00:17:44.670 --> 00:17:46.290
I beg your pardon!

00:17:55.360 --> 00:17:57.490
...have utterly defeated...

00:17:58.930 --> 00:18:00.100
defeated...

00:18:00.210 --> 00:18:01.850
Help me!

00:18:05.420 --> 00:18:06.820
Fear not.

00:18:07.840 --> 00:18:10.420
Who do you take me for?

00:18:20.280 --> 00:18:22.310
<i>Now I've done it!</i>

00:18:22.310 --> 00:18:24.750
<i>The Knight Alliance is going to kill me!</i>

00:18:25.570 --> 00:18:27.870
Th..thank you.

00:18:30.290 --> 00:18:31.880
What's this now?

00:18:32.800 --> 00:18:36.990
The soul of the knight is to save people
as part of our chivalrous duty.

00:18:36.990 --> 00:18:37.880
Right.

00:18:38.320 --> 00:18:42.370
I accidentally won this round, didn't I?

00:18:42.370 --> 00:18:44.890
Right. I lost.

00:18:45.370 --> 00:18:49.140
Yep! The knights still stand superior
over the commoners.

00:18:49.510 --> 00:18:51.010
That round's over.

00:18:52.840 --> 00:18:56.570
I, Musashi's knight Nate Argent Loup Mitotsudaira,

00:18:56.850 --> 00:19:01.390
wish to serve the Chancellor as the 5th Special Agent in

00:19:01.390 --> 00:19:03.950
Musashi Ariadust Academy's Supreme Federation.

00:19:04.260 --> 00:19:06.820
We're tied at one loss and one victory.

00:19:06.820 --> 00:19:08.960
Go on! It's your turn.

00:19:10.580 --> 00:19:15.230
Are you going to use your specialty, debate and oration?

00:19:16.330 --> 00:19:17.330
Masazumi!

00:19:25.130 --> 00:19:28.810
Okay, you may begin your strategy meetings.

00:19:29.330 --> 00:19:31.960
1:50 P.M.
Bridge, Eikoumaru

00:19:35.010 --> 00:19:38.490
Not watching the broadcast, former pupil?

00:19:38.490 --> 00:19:43.700
There's no need. We will profit from either outcome.

00:19:44.200 --> 00:19:46.410
If the Vice-president siding with the Council wins,

00:19:46.410 --> 00:19:48.510
Musashi along with everything else will be ours.

00:19:48.880 --> 00:19:52.280
If the Academy wins, we will go into war

00:19:52.280 --> 00:19:54.990
with Musashi and take everything.

00:19:55.720 --> 00:19:57.300
It's all the same.

00:19:58.830 --> 00:20:02.300
Wasn't this supposed to be about the princess?

00:20:02.690 --> 00:20:05.640
Her death will be forgotten by history.

00:20:07.520 --> 00:20:11.560
If she's an Armor of Deadly Sins, that simplifies matters.

00:20:11.560 --> 00:20:16.690
She can repent for Motonobu's sins
by offering herself up.

00:20:16.980 --> 00:20:21.200
Is that how you'll erase this whole affair
with Mikawa and the Armor?

00:20:21.200 --> 00:20:23.280
It'll have never happened!

00:20:23.670 --> 00:20:28.210
After all, history claims that Mikawa
was never meant to be eradicated.

00:20:29.570 --> 00:20:31.660
Show me the broadcast.

00:20:34.060 --> 00:20:36.490
I thought you didn't need to watch it.

00:20:36.920 --> 00:20:38.380
I changed my mind.

00:20:39.350 --> 00:20:42.380
I may have to step in.

00:20:42.600 --> 00:20:45.300
So then, let's begin the final face-off.

00:20:45.620 --> 00:20:48.000
Listen up. The rules of debate are...

00:20:51.000 --> 00:20:53.740
Mention your concerns and express your views.

00:20:53.740 --> 00:20:55.180
Whoever puts their opponent in a

00:20:55.180 --> 00:20:57.940
tight spot or convinces them you're right wins.

00:20:58.320 --> 00:21:01.440
Aoi, do you understand the position you're in?

00:21:01.440 --> 00:21:03.640
Y..yeah, you bet!

00:21:03.640 --> 00:21:05.700
D..don't underestimate me!

00:21:05.950 --> 00:21:08.660
How can you say that while trembling?

00:21:10.390 --> 00:21:13.580
I'm pretty dumb, so can I get help?

00:21:13.790 --> 00:21:16.990
Yeah, and I'll do the same if necessary.

00:21:17.430 --> 00:21:21.050
All set? Who will go first and second?

00:21:21.310 --> 00:21:23.320
I'll go first!

00:21:25.300 --> 00:21:27.890
Hey, hey! Why the silence?

00:21:27.890 --> 00:21:30.420
Going last is advantageous in a debate.

00:21:30.420 --> 00:21:31.810
It's common knowledge.

00:21:32.970 --> 00:21:34.290
For real?

00:21:34.290 --> 00:21:36.190
I'm willing to swap places.

00:21:37.290 --> 00:21:40.290
No thanks! I'm cool with going first! I'm first!

00:21:40.290 --> 00:21:43.030
Besides, I wanna hurry and get this crap over with!

00:21:43.540 --> 00:21:48.310
'Kay, guys. I, former Chancellor/President Tori Aoi,

00:21:48.310 --> 00:21:50.370
have a proposition regarding our situation.

00:21:50.640 --> 00:21:52.230
I just got one point.

00:21:52.680 --> 00:21:56.590
Retrieving our authority and stuff is merely a stepping stone

00:21:56.590 --> 00:21:58.960
towards my great plan to tell Horizon how I feel.

00:21:59.270 --> 00:22:01.340
So let's be real here.

00:22:01.600 --> 00:22:06.050
What do we have to gain or lose
by going to save Horizon?

00:22:07.680 --> 00:22:11.600
So I guess I should make my stance perfectly clear.

00:22:14.140 --> 00:22:15.390
I say...

00:22:20.130 --> 00:22:23.730
Why don't we just give up on going to save Horizon?

00:22:30.350 --> 00:22:31.700
Your food...

00:22:33.240 --> 00:22:37.250
Wh-wh-wh-wha...?

00:22:39.120 --> 00:22:42.550
What?!

00:22:44.700 --> 00:22:45.470
Huh?

00:22:46.100 --> 00:22:50.260
Sora ni nozomu you ni

00:22:46.100 --> 00:22:50.260
Our voyage across the real world

00:22:50.540 --> 00:22:57.270
Koukai suru genjitsu sekai no tabi

00:22:50.540 --> 00:22:57.270
Is like navigating straight for the sky

00:22:57.770 --> 00:23:01.610
Nani mo mottenai kedo

00:22:57.770 --> 00:23:01.610
I may not have anything

00:23:02.120 --> 00:23:04.720
Kokoro no naka

00:23:02.120 --> 00:23:04.720
But I have a dream

00:23:04.720 --> 00:23:08.950
Kagayaita yume ga aru yo

00:23:04.720 --> 00:23:08.950
That's shone brightly in my heart

00:23:09.200 --> 00:23:11.790
Mada kikoenai

00:23:09.200 --> 00:23:11.790
I still haven't heard

00:23:11.790 --> 00:23:15.280
Kimi no hontou no mune no koe

00:23:11.790 --> 00:23:15.280
The voice spoken from your heart

00:23:15.580 --> 00:23:20.200
Shiritain da — sugao wo misete yo

00:23:15.580 --> 00:23:20.200
Let me in — show me the real you

00:23:20.200 --> 00:23:23.790
Barabara ni chirabatta

00:23:20.200 --> 00:23:23.790
We'll bury the void

00:23:23.790 --> 00:23:26.890
Ikutsu mo no piisu wo

00:23:23.790 --> 00:23:26.890
As we find all of the pieces

00:23:27.060 --> 00:23:29.560
Hitotsu zutsu sagashite

00:23:27.060 --> 00:23:29.560
That have gotten scattered around

00:23:29.560 --> 00:23:32.720
Kuuhaku wo umete iku no sa

00:23:29.560 --> 00:23:32.720
One piece at a time

00:23:32.720 --> 00:23:37.540
Ubawareta kimi no egao

00:23:32.720 --> 00:23:37.540
Your smile has been stolen

00:23:37.540 --> 00:23:41.210
Tori modosu tame ni hashiru yo

00:23:37.540 --> 00:23:41.210
But I will race to get it back

00:23:41.210 --> 00:23:47.150
Boku wa hikari sasu michi wo

00:23:41.210 --> 00:23:47.150
As I run down the shining path

00:24:07.110 --> 00:24:10.950
Next Episode
"Ruler of the Land"
